  "title": "KV checkpoint and release separate tree ownership from request allocation",
  "mechanism": "checkpoint_kv_cache requires an unfinished request, optionally publishes through tree_cache.checkpoint and advances prefix_len even when insertion is skipped. release_kv_cache first handles a Mamba-only allocation or a streaming session that claims the row. On the normal path it optionally checkpoints owned KV, requiring a finished request for a Mamba tree, then frees only the request-owned suffix after cache_protected_len, unlocks the tree, releases overallocation, calls on_release, frees the request row and marks KV released. Paged extension computes a conservative demand with per-request page and shard headroom, passes that estimate to get_extend_allocation_demand and evicts the returned demand, which need not equal the conservative estimate. The subsequent allocator result is checked and a missing allocation raises a visible prefill OOM error.",
  "corrections": [
    "The conservative estimate is an input to the allocator demand function, not necessarily the exact eviction request.",
    "A checkpoint preserves a tree-owned prefix; releasing a request must not free that protected prefix.",
    "Whole-file citations were replaced with the specific ownership and allocation branches; native hashing and speculative allocation claims are not included in this subset."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
